# Test: with a daemon listening and no credentials to log in to it, `show
#       host trend` refuses with "a ze listens ..., but this account has no
#       credentials" and the fix that asks from an account that can log in.
# QUESTION: does an operator whose account holds no credentials, on a box
#   whose daemon runs, read that cause and its fix, and never `ze start`?
# VALIDATES: AC-32 of spec-host-resource-trend-alerts. runBGP
#   (internal/component/cli/client/main.go) hands the offline fallback the
#   cause unansweredWithoutCredentials built: the walk
#   sshclient.UnreachedWithoutCredentials probes the listener, finds the
#   daemon, and stops at the credentials step.
# PREVENTS: "show host trend needs the daemon, and no daemon answered" with
#   `fix: ze start` while the daemon runs, which sends the operator to start a
#   second daemon.
# Why not a unit test: TestOfflineCauseCredentialsUnavailableFollowsTheListener
#   proves the classification against a bare TCP listener; only the real
#   client beside the real daemon proves the operator meets it.
#
# The environment names the daemon's port and no user or password, and the
# test's store holds no login, so the credentials cannot be loaded.
# The daemon setup is test/plugin/host-trend-show.ci's.

option=needs-linux
option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT
tmpfs=running.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# "Ze running." is printed after the SSH listener accepts.
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start running.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze cli -c "show host trend":exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=show host trend needs the daemon, and a ze listens at 127.0.0.1
expect=stderr:contains=but this account has no credentials to log in to it
expect=stderr:contains=fix: ze cli --user <name> -c "show host trend"
reject=stderr:contains=fix: ze start
reject=stderr:contains=no daemon answered
